<title>USA: TABLE - Chester Valley Q4 net increases.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Chester Valley Q4 net increases.</headline>
<dateline>DOWNINGTOWN, Pa. 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended Twelve Months Ended</p>
<p>						    June 30,  June 30,</p>
<p>					   1997    1996    1997    1996</p>
<p> Net interest income		 2,972  2,498  11,066   9,691</p>
<p>Provision for possible loan losses</p>
<p>					     166     93     523     340</p>
<p> SAIF special assessment		--     --   1,387	--</p>
<p> Net income				740    601   1,926   2,439</p>
<p>Earnings per common share</p>
<p>   Primary				0.36   0.29    0.93    1.18</p>
<p>   Fully Diluted			0.36   0.29    0.93    1.18</p>
<p>(Dollars in Thousands Except for Per Share Amounts)</p>
<p>NOTE: Chester Valley Bancorp Inc said its fiscal year ended June 30.</p>
<p>The company said its per share amounts have been restated to reflect the effects of the five percent stock dividend paid in September 1996 and the March 1997 five-for-four stock split effected in the form of a dividend.</p>
